# Always refresh the installable APK

When TrustID changes are production-ready (especially web UX, auth, ambient scan, device plugins):

1. Follow deploy-after-production (commit + push `main` ? Netlify).
2. Rebuild the debug APK so the user can reinstall without hunting Gradle output:

```bash
npm run android:apk -w @trustid/device
```

3. The build must leave a stable file at:

```text
TrustID-debug.apk
```

in the repo root (`c:\Users\Hp\Desktop\TRUST ID\TrustID-debug.apk`).

4. Do this without waiting to be asked — the user installs by tapping that same file.

## Live web updates (already in Capacitor)

The APK loads `https://trustedid.netlify.app` by default (`CAP_USE_LIVE_WEB` ? `0`).
Web/UI/auth features update on app launch after Netlify deploy — no reinstall needed.

Rebuild the APK when:

- native Android/iOS plugin code changes
- Capacitor config / permissions / manifest change
- the user asks for a fresh installable binary
- first-time setup or live URL / signing changes

Do not rebuild for docs-only or API-only changes that never affect the device shell.
